cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Supply-Droop Detection With an All-Digital Dynamic Variation Monitor and Corner-Calibrated Thresholds"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Patel
    given-names: Krish Badal
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Science, Bengaluru"
  - family-names: Govindu
    given-names: Vignesh
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Science, Bengaluru"
date-released: 2026-11-21
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vignesh-GMAXX/DVM-Supply-Droop-Detector"
abstract: >-
  Transistor-level, post-layout implementation of the all-digital dynamic
  variation monitor (DVM) of Bowman et al. in a generic 45-nm process
  (gpdk045), with TAP_CAL, a per-die tap-calibration block that removes all
  no-droop false alarms across 15 process-temperature corners.
keywords:
  - dynamic variation monitor
  - supply voltage droop
  - time-to-digital converter
  - tunable replica circuit
  - calibration
